\name{cellucid_field_restore}
\alias{cellucid_field_restore}
\title{Restore a deleted field}
\usage{
cellucid_field_restore(viewer, field, which)
}
\arguments{
\item{viewer}{A viewer \code{\link{cellucid_view}()} or \code{\link{cellucid_serve}()} returned.}
\item{field}{The deleted field by the name it had when deleted. A named list. Required. \describe{\item{\code{key}}{The field or gene name as the app shows it. Text (at least 1 character). Required.}\item{\code{source}}{"obs" for a column of the cells, "var" for a gene. One of \code{"obs"}, \code{"var"}. Required.}}}
\item{which}{Only when several deleted fields have this name: which, 1 the first of them as Deleted fields lists them. A whole number (at least 1). Left out unless given (the viewer then chooses as its own control does).}
}
\value{
A \code{cellucid_action_request}, at once and invisibly: the action is sent now, or when the viewer's channel opens.
\code{\link{cellucid_action_result}(request)} returns its outcome (what it did, as names, counts and ids), or \code{NULL} when it had nothing to report; \code{request$step} is the history step it made.
}
\description{
Bring back a deleted field under its name, as it was when deleted.
}
\details{
The viewer's action \code{field.restore} (Fields). It changes the viewer's state: one step of the viewer's history, labeled as R's, undone like any other. The state it can change: \code{field-overlays}, \code{active-field}, \code{filters}, \code{colors}, \code{highlights}, \code{views}.
}
\seealso{
\code{\link{cellucid_act}()} sends any action by its type, and \code{\link{cellucid_action_result}()}
collects its answer.
}
\examples{
if (interactive() && requireNamespace("SeuratObject", quietly = TRUE)) {
  data("pbmc_small", package = "SeuratObject")
  viewer <- cellucid_view(SeuratObject::UpdateSeuratObject(pbmc_small))
  request <- cellucid_field_restore(viewer, field = list(key = "cell_type",
      source = "obs"))
  print(request)
  # cellucid_action_result(request) waits for its outcome.
  cellucid_stop(viewer)
}
}
